  "caveats": [
    "minVersion 0 means the directive predates upstream's per-directive version annotations (older than every distro listed here).",
    "Distro vendors (notably RHEL) backport features into older version numbers; a 'no' cell can be a 'yes' on a specific minor release. Always confirm on the target with `systemd-analyze verify` and `systemctl show -p <Directive> <unit>`.",
    "systemd ignores unknown directives with a log warning and still starts the unit, so an unsupported hardening line silently provides no protection."
  ],
